# Dual-path architecture: runtime NER + operations Ask LEO

This codebase has TWO parallel code paths that process clinical entities.
Any change to assertions, semantic tags, safety guards, or LLM prompt rules
MUST be applied to BOTH paths or the system will behave inconsistently.

## Path 1 — NER runtime pipeline (coding worker)

Processes encounters at ingestion time.

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| LLM extraction prompt | `libs/prompts/extraction_v1.py` |
| Assertion validation | `services/coding_worker/app/pipeline/llm_extractor.py` (`_VALID_ASSERTIONS`) |
| Schema mapping | `libs/ner/schema_mapper.py` (assertion allowlist in `_map_entity`) |
| Extractor contract | `libs/ner/extractor_contract.py` |
| Lab-value guard | `libs/ner/lab_value_guard.py` |
| Scope guard | `libs/ner/scope_guard.py` |
| ConText engine | `libs/ner/context_engine.py` |
| Tier classifier | `libs/coding_engine/tier_classifier.py` (`_AUTO_CODE_BLOCKED`) |
| Pipeline orchestrator | `services/coding_worker/app/pipeline/pipeline_service.py` |

## Path 2 — /operations Ask LEO (review UI)

Processes CodingReview nodes when a reviewer clicks "Ask LEO".

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Escalation prompts | `libs/llm_client/escalation.py` (`_CANDIDATES_SYSTEM`, `escalate_coding`) |
| Ask LEO smart endpoint | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`ask_leo_smart`) |
| Ask LEO rank endpoint | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`ask_leo_rank_candidates`, inline prompt) |
| Disorder verifier | `libs/llm_client/disorder_verifier.py` (`_SYSTEM_PROMPT`) |
| Assertion notes | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`_ASSERTION_NOTES`) |
| Assertion validation | `services/api/app/routers/training.py` (`_VALID_ASSERTIONS`) |
| Label verifier | `services/api/app/services/label_verifier.py` (`_AUTO_CODE_BLOCKED`, `_ASSERTION_QUEUE_SET`) |

## Shared graph + UI

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Document writes | `libs/cypher/documents_queries.py` (`_NON_PRESENT`, `_assertion_context`) |
| Coding review queries | `libs/cypher/coding_review_queries.py` (assertion filters) |
| UI assertion options | `services/ui/src/components/operations/CodingReviewCasesModal.tsx` (`ASSERTION_OPTIONS`) |
| UI assertion chips | `services/ui/src/lib/types.ts` (`ASSERTION_CHIP`), `services/ui/src/components/AssertionChip.tsx` |
| Training adapter | `libs/model_registry/training_adapter.py` (`_VALID_ASSERTIONS`) |

## Checklist for ANY assertion / safety-guard / prompt change

1. Update the runtime extraction prompt (`libs/prompts/extraction_v1.py`)
2. Update the escalation prompts (`libs/llm_client/escalation.py`)
3. Update the ask-leo-rank inline prompt (`training.py`)
4. Update ALL `_VALID_ASSERTIONS` sets (at least 3 locations)
5. Update `_AUTO_CODE_BLOCKED` sets (at least 2 locations)
6. Update `_ASSERTION_QUEUE_SET` if the assertion needs human review
7. Update `_assertion_context()` in `documents_queries.py`
8. Update `_NON_PRESENT` if the assertion should block patient-level shortcuts
9. Update assertion review queue Cypher filters if needed
10. Update UI: `ASSERTION_OPTIONS`, `ASSERTION_CHIP`, `AssertionChip.tsx`
11. Update ConText engine if the assertion can be detected from text patterns
12. Add tests covering both paths
